  "assumptions": [
    "Illustrative durable broker and ledger; consumer failure does not erase a committed append.",
    "Broker acknowledgment and ledger effect share no transaction; there is no duplicate protection.",
    "One processing slot per consumer, freed on effect commit/cancellation; early ACK does not free it.",
    "Only the current lease token strictly before its deadline is accepted; this is model policy, not an SQS guarantee.",
    "Expiry permits another delivery without fencing running work; dead-lettering does not erase effects.",
    "Transport delay is zero except configured ACK delay; selected transport loss precedes token validation.",
    "Same-time phases: effects, expiry, ACK, crash, recovery/enqueue, dispatch; same-phase insertion order.",
    "Recovery actions are initially scheduled before message enqueues; dispatch uses availability then input order.",
    "Pending ACK includes planned ACK-after-effect. Scheduled times are not observed completions.",
    "Completed means settled, not business success; confirmed ACK-without-effect is unknown on limited prefixes.",
    "Producer failures, broker loss/replication, lease extension, backoff and external providers are excluded.",
    "Seed is replay metadata; no random choices. External wall guards may censor differently across machines."
  ],
